      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried adding your suggested change to the firmware by modifying board.h like so:\n\n#undef CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_ADDR\n\n#undef CONFIG_RW_SIG_ADDR\n\n#define CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_STORAGE_OFF \\\n\t(CONFIG_RO_STORAGE_OFF + CONFIG_RO_SIZE - CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_SIZE)\n#define CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_ADDR (CONFIG_MAPPED_STORAGE_BASE + \\\n\tCONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_OFF + CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_STORAGE_OFF)\n\n#define CONFIG_RW_SIZE                                          \\\n\t((NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE / CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE) * \\\n\t CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE)\n\t \nAdding storage definitions that include CONFIG_MAPPED_STORAGE_BASE to header files like board.h cause the size of the ec.bin file to blow up to 1GB. Please see b:273569976 comments #3-#7 for background and let me know if you have suggestions to work around the problem and still remove the #ifdef from runtime code.",
